kind: fix
Two leaks in the array-backed broadphase tree, which CollisionScene.collides
builds once per call to find its candidate pairs, so a long-running caller
grew without bound (tests/test_invariants.py::test_calls_hold_no_memory):
- HierarchyTree::init_0 through init_3 each call clear(), which frees
  `nodes` and allocates a fresh array of 16, then assign `nodes` a new
  array of 2n without freeing those 16: about 1.6 KB a tree. Free them first.
- DynamicAABBTreeArrayCollisionManager::registerObjects allocates its
  leaves with new[] and never frees them, though dtree.init copies them into
  the tree's own nodes: a node per object. Free them once copied.
Not yet reported upstream; the same lines are in coal devel as pinned.
--- a/include/coal/broadphase/detail/hierarchy_tree_array-inl.h
+++ b/include/coal/broadphase/detail/hierarchy_tree_array-inl.h
@@ -100,6 +100,9 @@
 
   n_leaves = (size_t)n_leaves_;
   root_node = NULL_NODE;
+  //// TRIMKIT PATCH: fix.hierarchy-tree-array-leak
+  delete[] nodes;  // the 16 nodes clear() just allocated
+  //// TRIMKIT END PATCH
   nodes = new Node[n_leaves * 2];
   std::copy(leaves, leaves + n_leaves, nodes);
   freelist = n_leaves;
@@ -125,6 +128,9 @@
 
